# Spec Kit

QLMED uses Spec Kit as the only feature-governance engine. GSD stays disabled.

**Before changing behavior, contracts, permissions, persistence, integrations or architecture:**

1. Read `governance.yaml` for the pinned version and validator.
2. Read `.specify/memory/constitution.md`.
3. Read or create the feature under `specs/`.
4. Use the project skills in `.cursor/skills/speckit-*` (same content as `.agents/skills/speckit-*`).
5. Do not bump the Spec Kit pin on `main`. Upgrade only on a disposable branch, keep QLMED customizations, then `npm run docs:validate`.

Work in a task-specific git worktree. Do not edit an unrelated dirty checkout.

If this worktree has no `graphify-out/graph.json`, query the canonical checkout graph with `--graph ../app/graphify-out/graph.json` or `--graph ../app-dev/graphify-out/graph.json` before exploring code.
